{"audio": "ephesians-06.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 154933, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 1600, "text": "Ephesians, Chapter Six."}, {"start_ms": 1600, "end_ms": 5467, "text": "Children, obey your parents in the Lord: for this is right."}, {"start_ms": 5467, "end_ms": 13067, "text": "Honour thy father and mother; (which is the first commandment with promise;) That it may be well with thee, and thou mayest live long on the earth."}, {"start_ms": 13067, "end_ms": 19600, "text": "And, ye fathers, provoke not your children to wrath: but bring them up in the nurture and admonition of the Lord."}, {"start_ms": 19600, "end_ms": 37067, "text": "Servants, be obedient to them that are your masters according to the flesh, with fear and trembling, in singleness of your heart, as unto Christ; Not with eyeservice, as menpleasers; but as the servants of Christ, doing the will of God from the heart; With good will doing service, as to the Lord,"}, {"start_ms": 37067, "end_ms": 45467, "text": "and not to men: Knowing that whatsoever good thing any man doeth, the same shall he receive of the Lord, whether he be bond or free."}, {"start_ms": 45467, "end_ms": 55333, "text": "And, ye masters, do the same things unto them, forbearing threatening: knowing that your Master also is in heaven; neither is there respect of persons with him."}, {"start_ms": 55333, "end_ms": 59867, "text": "Finally, my brethren, be strong in the Lord, and in the power of his might."}, {"start_ms": 59867, "end_ms": 65733, "text": "Put on the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to stand against the wiles of the devil."}, {"start_ms": 65733, "end_ms": 75733, "text": "For we wrestle not against flesh and blood, but against principalities, against powers, against the rulers of the darkness of this world, against spiritual wickedness in high places."}, {"start_ms": 75733, "end_ms": 84800, "text": "Wherefore take unto you the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to withstand in the evil day, and having done all, to stand."}, {"start_ms": 84800, "end_ms": 100000, "text": "Stand therefore, having your loins girt about with truth, and having on the breastplate of righteousness; And your feet shod with the preparation of the gospel of peace; Above all, taking the shield of faith, wherewith ye shall be able to quench all the fiery darts of the wicked."}, {"start_ms": 100000, "end_ms": 115467, "text": "And take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God: Praying always with all prayer and supplication in the Spirit, and watching thereunto with all perseverance and supplication for all saints; And for me, that utterance may be given unto me,"}, {"start_ms": 115467, "end_ms": 125600, "text": "that I may open my mouth boldly, to make known the mystery of the gospel, For which I am an ambassador in bonds: that therein I may speak boldly, as I ought to speak."}, {"start_ms": 125600, "end_ms": 143200, "text": "But that ye also may know my affairs, and how I do, Tychicus, a beloved brother and faithful minister in the Lord, shall make known to you all things: Whom I have sent unto you for the same purpose, that ye might know our affairs, and that he might comfort your hearts."}, {"start_ms": 143200, "end_ms": 148400, "text": "Peace be to the brethren, and love with faith, from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ."}, {"start_ms": 148400, "end_ms": 152533, "text": "Grace be with all them that love our Lord Jesus Christ in sincerity."}, {"start_ms": 152533, "end_ms": 154933, "text": "Amen."}], "words": [{"t": "Ephesians,", "s": 223, "e": 810, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 891, "e": 1195, "si": 0}, {"t": "Six.", "s": 1276, "e": 1499, "si": 0}, {"t": "Children,", "s": 1961, "e": 2381, "si": 1}, {"t": "obey", "s": 2722, "e": 2942, "si": 1}, {"t": "your", "s": 2962, "e": 3083, "si": 1}, {"t": "parents", "s": 3123, "e": 3523, "si": 1}, {"t": "in", "s": 3644, "e": 3744, "si": 1}, {"t": "the", "s": 3784, "e": 3864, "si": 1}, {"t":